WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.020
Reactions were mixed after Felix Tshisekedi
was announced the winner.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:13.600
From jubilation 
to consternation, people certainly made their

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.390
feelings known.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.650
The opposition leader wasn't expected to win
the Presidential vote in the Democratic Republic

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.130
of Congo.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.150
But he edged out his main rival, putting the
country on course for its first democratic

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:32.630
transfer of power in almost 60 years since
independence.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:41.360
I know many of you find it hard to accept
- but I say it with sincerity, I pay homage

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:46.830
to President Joseph Kabila, President of the
Republic...

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:55.550
Today, we must no longer consider each other
as adversaries but rather as partners in democratic

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:58.960
change in our country.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:04.040
Some believe Tshisekedi won by cutting a deal
with President Joseph Kabila, who's clung

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.119
to power for 18 years.

00:01:07.119 --> 00:01:12.280
Although Kabila's preferred candidate only
came third, the man expected to win, Martin

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:21.979
Fayulu, is among many contesting 
the results.

00:01:21.979 --> 00:01:28.810
These results do not reflect the truth of
the ballots.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:36.179
This is obviously an unacceptable electoral
fraud of a nature that will provoke general

00:01:36.179 --> 00:01:39.689
chaos across the country.

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:45.200
Meanwhile, the country's influential Catholic
church is already questioning the vote.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:50.319
It says official results do not match the
outcome compiled by its 40,000 observers at

00:01:50.319 --> 00:01:53.159
all polling stations across the troubled country.

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:55.420
The church has also called for calm.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:57.749
Still, many people are upset.

00:01:57.749 --> 00:02:04.380
In Goma, many did not hide their feelings
amid the potential for unrest.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:09.189
We don't want this Machiavellian sale of the
Congolese people's power.

00:02:09.189 --> 00:02:18.010
We are going to call on Article 64 of our
Constitution.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:03:53.359
In the end, though, experts say it will be
up to the country's constitutional

00:03:53.359 --> 00:04:06.409
court

00:04:06.409 --> 00:04:23.310
to rule 
on

00:04:23.310 --> 00:05:22.669
the vote.

